  "summary": "I worked through all 8 items in your results inbox and the 5 that arrived while I was working. 12 are closed. One is deliberately left open: the chest X-ray for Leslie Parisian (pt-0007), because only a preliminary report exists so far.\n\n**Original items:**\n- **pt-0006 Raj Patel – CT abdomen/pelvis 10/19:** Nothing explains the hematuria. It showed a 4 mm left lower lobe nodule that is already being followed in his lung cancer screening. I first ordered the yearly screening low-dose CT for Mar–May 2027, with a tracking task, a patient message and a note. A later arrival changed this (see below). Closed.\n- **pt-0016 Edra Ondricka – TSH:** 2.1, normal. Closed.\n- **pt-0016 Edra Ondricka – potassium:** The lab corrected the 6.3 to 4.4, which is normal, so nothing was needed. Closed.\n- **pt-0007 Leslie Parisian – CT angiogram 10/20 (preliminary read):** The final report shows no PE, and the preliminary \"nodule\" is a blood vessel. The radiologist says no follow-up is needed, which also satisfies RBC-RAD-05. Closed.\n- **pt-0007 Leslie Parisian – BMP 10/22:** Creatinine went from 0.98 to 1.64 within 48 hours, which meets the policy's AKI rule. I ordered an urgent repeat BMP for by Mon 10/26, messaged him, and wrote a note. The note flags his PRN naproxen for your review. Closed.\n- **pt-0064 Helen Marchetti – ED BMP 9/26:** Creatinine 1.36 had no earlier value in the window to compare against, so it didn't meet the AKI rule. Closed with no action.\n- **pt-0033 Carol Whitfield – BMP 10/22:** Creatinine 1.31 doesn't meet the AKI rule. I didn't use the 10/21 value (0.84) because it was marked entered in error. Closed.\n- **pt-0008 Walter Brennan – potassium 6.4:** The lab first flagged the sample as hemolyzed. I ordered an urgent repeat BMP, messaged him and wrote a note. A later correction changed this (see below).\n\n**Items that arrived while I worked:**\n- **pt-0008 Walter Brennan – lab correction:** The sample was not hemolyzed, so the 6.4 is real. I switched to the critical-potassium protocol:\n  - Notified on-call at stat priority. My first message gave the wrong order ID, so I sent a correction.\n  - Ordered a stat BMP for today.\n  - Reviewed his medications: none raise potassium, so nothing was held.\n  - Sent him a corrected message asking him to come in today, and wrote a note.\n- **pt-0006 Raj Patel – addendum to his April screening CT:** A second reader found a new 5 mm right upper lobe nodule. It is now Lung-RADS 3, with a repeat low-dose CT due 6 months after the April scan. I ordered that CT for by 11/14, set a tracking task due 11/14, sent him a corrected message, and wrote a note explaining the change.\n- **pt-0033 Carol Whitfield – creatinine 1.78 (urgent care, 10/22 evening):** This is up from 1.31 that morning, which meets the AKI rule. I ordered an urgent repeat BMP for by 10/26, messaged her, and wrote a note.\n- **pt-0064 Helen Marchetti – creatinine 1.48 (urgent care 10/22):** This is up from 0.88 on 10/21, which meets the AKI rule. I ordered an urgent repeat BMP for by 10/26, messaged her, and wrote a note.\n- **pt-0007 Leslie Parisian – chest X-ray 10/22:** The preliminary read shows a possible 7 mm right upper lobe nodule. Policy says to act only on the final report, and none has been issued, so this item is still open.\n\n**Needs you:**\n1. My tools can't cancel lab or imaging orders, so I created tasks for you to discontinue two superseded orders:\n   - Mr. Brennan's urgent repeat BMP, now replaced by today's stat order.\n   - Mr. Patel's March–May 2027 screening CT and its tracking task, now replaced by the CT due by 11/14.\n2. Your messages queue has 6 open refill requests that I didn't touch, since this request covered only the results inbox.",
